  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "sprite s in the left area whose color appears on the right frame",
  "dst": "center at positions d in the right frame",
  "match_cond": "s.color == d.same_row_frame_edges.color and s.color == d.same_col_frame_edges.color",
  "multi_step": "move sprites from bottom to top, with new covering old"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10-15 rows × 14-20 cols
  bg: 0
  layout: left sprite strip | divider column | rectangular frame on right
  divider:
    single column of uniform non-bg color spanning full grid height
    separates sprite strip from frame
  frame:
    base_color: single non-bg color (≠ divider, ≠ any sprite color)
    rectangle spanning full grid height; width = interior_w + 2
    edges: top==bottom mirrored, left==right mirrored
    markers: mover colors placed at matching positions on both opposite edges
    interior: 8-13 rows × 8-13 cols, filled with bg
    extra non-matching colors on edges [observed]
  sprites:
    count: 2-3 movers + 0-1 distractors = 2-4 total
    shape: 8-connected single-color blob, 3-9 pixels, bbox 1-5 × 1-5
    colors: all distinct, ≠ bg, ≠ frame_base, ≠ divider
    placed in left strip (cols 0..divider-1), no mutual overlap
    movers: color has matching markers on both L/R and T/B frame edges
    distractors: color absent from frame edge markers; unchanged in output
  markers:
    per mover: 1-2 row marks × 1-2 col marks
    row mark: both L and R frame edges have mover's color at that row
    col mark: both T and B frame edges have mover's color at that col
    no two movers share a row mark or col mark
  transformation:
    erase movers from left strip
    stamp each mover centered at Cartesian product of row_marks × col_marks
    order: bottom-to-top by input position (lower stamped first, upper covers)
    pixels clipped to frame interior
    distractors unchanged

generation_strategy:
  1. Sample H=10-15, interior_h=H-2, interior_w=8-13, sprite_area_w=3-5
  2. W = sprite_area_w + 1 (divider) + interior_w + 2; reject if W not in 14-20
  3. Assign distinct colors: divider, frame_base, movers (2-3), distractors (0-1)
  4. Generate sprites via random walk (8-connected, 3-9 pixels, bbox ≤ 5 × sprite_area_w)
  5. Per mover: pick 1-2 row marks and 1-2 col marks in interior; spacing ≥ sprite dim; no mark reuse across movers; verify sprite centered at each target fits in interior
  6. Build frame: top/bottom edges = frame_base with mover colors at col marks (mirrored); L/R edges = frame_base with mover colors at row marks (mirrored)
  7. Place sprites in left strip top-to-bottom with random vertical gaps; add divider column
  8. Validate: bg is most-common color, main(input) ≠ input, main(input) runs without error
```
